ti-run side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics in the Dashboard. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 | **Consolidated** with HLR-1 (redundant/overlapping HLR): the \"diff view\" is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run parameters and metrics — same component (Dashboard), same team, same UI surface and data. Per the redundant-HLR rule it is ONE capability covered by a single epic at the higher priority (P0); splitting would produce two epics building the same surface plus an artificial serialization edge. The P1 label reads as relative value, not a deferral signal. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 | Direct: registered model versions link back to the producing run; comparison openable from the Model Registry. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E003 | Docs-authoring epic exempt from priority inheritance; priority derived from strategy frontmatter (Major → P1). Covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Component Mapping\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Classification | Handling |\n|--------------------|---------------------|----------------|----------|\n| Dashboard | Dashboard | Active (code changes) | E001 |\n| Model Registry | Model Registry | Active (code changes) | E002 |\n| Data Science Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive (listed as affected, no changes described; pipeline runs are already surfaced in the Dashboard per `architecture/rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md`) | Validation becomes an acceptance criterion on E001: the comparison must render parameters and metrics for Data Science Pipelines runs as well as training runs. Same platform, so no separate validation epic. |\n| (docs work) | Documentation | Active (content authoring) | E003 — substantive new doc topics are a distinct work stream, not an incidental touch-up. |\n\nAll canonical names are verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`; no\nnon-obvious mappings were needed.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing refinement sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no\n   Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance\n   criteria, no NFRs, and the Affected Components section is a bare list\n   without per-component change/owner detail. Team assignments were derived\n   from architecture-context owning teams; ACs were derived from HLRs.\n2. **Docs epic team assumption**: E003 is assigned to RHOAI Dashboard by\n   default (primary documented surface); the Documentation component has no\n   owning team recorded in the architecture context.\n3. **Docs priority vs HLR label**: HLR-4 is labeled P2 while E003 is P1 —\n   intentional, per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority\n   Major → P1).\n4. **Passive-component assumption**: Data Science Pipelines is treated as\n   passive — the Dashboard already surfaces pipeline runs (KFP v2 API per\n   `data-science-pipelines.md`), so comparison of pipeline-run parameters and\n   metrics is expected to need no DSP-side changes. If E001's validation AC\n   fails (pipeline run metadata not accessible in a comparable shape), a\n   follow-up Data Science Pipelines epic is required — this is an\n   implementation-detail risk, not a genuine unknown (the strategy flags no\n   open questions).\n5. **Priority inversions**: none detected — HLR priorities are consistent with\n   the technical scope.\n\nNo epic exceeds ~2 weeks of estimated effort; no re-split triggers recorded.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\nin-platform across components already at GA maturity.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23831,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b9438ff936d69a5","agent_id":"aaf38669ceccb3185","session_id":"f1c0923d-cf0e-4d69-ac1b-c20ed66527c8","uuid":"3212bc97-df0e-4913-ad75-53f6831b2716","timestamp":"2