{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-839084f4b5b1fb32","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n10\t\n11\tThe strategy adds run comparison to the platform: users select two or more\n12\ttraining or pipeline runs and view parameters and metrics side by side (with a\n13\tdiff mode between two runs) in the Dashboard, registered model versions link\n14\tback to the run that produced them so a comparison can be opened from the\n15\tModel Registry, and the workflow is documented.\n16\t\n17\t**Triage (Step 0):** not below-threshold and not docs-only. The strategy spans\n18\tmultiple active components (Dashboard, Model Registry) and multiple distinct\n19\twork streams (Dashboard UI implementation, Model Registry metadata/linkage\n20\twork, and substantive documentation authoring per HLR-4), so the multi-epic\n21\tpath applies.\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n26\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Registered model version linkage to producing run | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Documentation for the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n30\t\n31\tNotes on epic assignments:\n32\t\n33\t- **Teams** derive from the architecture-context owning teams\n34\t  (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` → RHOAI Dashboard,\n35\t  `architecture/rhoai-3.0/model-registry.md` → Model Registry). The strategy\n36\t  provides no Impacted Teams table (see Health Warnings).\n37\t- **E003 team** is assigned to RHOAI Dashboard (the primary documented surface)\n38\t  because the Documentation component has no owning team in the architecture\n39\t  context; confirm with docs owners before scheduling.\n40\t- **E003 priority** is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception: the\n41\t  strategy frontmatter priority is Major → P1, overriding the P2 label on\n42\t  HLR-4 (see HLR Traceability Matrix).\n43\t\n44\t## Dependency DAG\n45\t\n46\t```mermaid\n47\tgraph TD\n48\t    E001[\"E001 Run comparison view (Dashboard)\"] --> E002[\"E002 Model version run linkage (Model Registry)\"]\n49\t    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Comparison workflow documentation\"]\n50\t    E002 --> E003\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\tCritical path: E001 → E002 → E003 (length 3).\n54\t\n55\t## DAG Justification\n56\t\n57\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n58\t|------|------|-----------|\n59\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (artifact another epic builds against) | HLR-2's deliverable is not just storing a run link on a model version — it is \"a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry\". That entry point builds against the run-comparison surface E001 introduces; shipping it first would produce a dead affordance. The linkage storage itself is independent work inside the same epic. |\n60\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the comparison workflow delivered by the Dashboard implementation; docs-authoring is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n61\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | HLR-4 requires docs to cover the workflow \"from both the runs list and the registry\", so the docs must also follow the Model Registry implementation. |\n62\t\n63\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics: all three\n64\taffected components exist in the architecture context and are already Konflux\n65\tonboarded, and no new component or external dependency is introduced. No\n66\tInvestigation epics: the strategy states \"Open Questions: None\" and no\n67\tconditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks tables are present.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n70\t\n71\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Analysis |\n72\t|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n73\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Direct: multi-run side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics in the Dashboard. |\n74\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 | **Consolidated** with HLR-1 (redundant/overlapping HLR): the \"diff view\" is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run parameters and metrics — same component (Dashboard), same team, same UI surface and data. Per the redundant-HLR rule it is ONE capability covered by a single epic at the higher priority (P0); splitting would produce two epics building the same surface plus an artificial serialization edge. The P1 label reads as relative value, not a deferral signal. |\n75\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 | Direct: registered model versions link back to the producing run; comparison openable from the Model Registry. |\n76\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E003 | Docs-authoring epic exempt from priority inheritance; priority derived from strategy frontmatter (Major → P1). Covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry. |\n77\t\n78\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n79\t\n80\t## Component Mapping\n81\t\n82\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Classification | Handling |\n83\t|--------------------|---------------------|----------------|----------|\n84\t| Dashboard | Dashboard | Active (code changes) | E001 |\n85\t| Model Registry | Model Registry | Active (code changes) | E002 |\n86\t| Data Science Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive (listed as affected, no changes described; pipeline runs are already surfaced in the Dashboard per `architecture/rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md`) | Validation becomes an acceptance criterion on E001: the comparison must render parameters and metrics for Data Science Pipelines runs as well as training runs. Same platform, so no separate validation epic. |\n87\t| (docs work) | Documentation | Active (content authoring) | E003 — substantive new doc topics are a distinct work stream, not an incidental touch-up. |\n88\t\n89\tAll canonical names are verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`; no\n90\tnon-obvious mappings were needed.\n91\t\n92\t## Health Warnings\n93\t\n94\t1. **Missing refinement sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no\n95\t   Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance\n96\t   criteria, no NFRs, and the Affected Components section is a bare list\n97\t   without per-component change/owner detail. Team assignments were derived\n98\t   from architecture-context owning teams; ACs were derived from HLRs.\n99\t2. **Docs epic team assumption**: E003 is assigned to RHOAI Dashboard by\n100\t   default (primary documented surface); the Documentation component has no\n101\t   owning team recorded in the architecture context.\n102\t3. **Docs priority vs HLR label**: HLR-4 is labeled P2 while E003 is P1 —\n103\t   intentional, per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority\n104\t   Major → P1).\n105\t4. **Passive-component assumption**: Data Science Pipelines is treated as\n106\t   passive — the Dashboard already surfaces pipeline runs (KFP v2 API per\n107\t   `data-science-pipelines.md`), so comparison of pipeline-run parameters and\n108\t   metrics is expected to need no DSP-side changes. If E001's validation AC\n109\t   fails (pipeline run metadata not accessible in a comparable shape), a\n110\t   follow-up Data Science Pipelines epic is required — this is an\n111\t   implementation-detail risk, not a genuine unknown (the strategy flags no\n112\t   open questions).\n113\t5. **Priority inversions**: none detected — HLR priorities are consistent with\n114\t   the technical scope.\n115\t\n116\tNo epic exceeds ~2 weeks of estimated effort; no re-split triggers recorded.\n117\t\n118\t## Tiered Delivery\n119\t\n120\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n121\tin-platform across components already at GA maturity.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e298cc7fa9244b","agent_id":"a2addad5e24cf88cd","session_id":"f1c0923d-cf0e-4d69-ac1b-c20ed66527c8","uuid":"6f7015ef-22f6-46de-a635-834e9a411863","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:38.837Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-839084f4b5b1fb32","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
