{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1139a8599b4dd4f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n3\ttitle: Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run comparison view for training and pipeline runs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a run comparison view in the Dashboard. Users can select\n34\ttwo or more runs from the runs list and view their parameters and metrics side\n35\tby side, and when exactly two runs are selected the comparison highlights\n36\twhich parameters and metrics changed between them. The comparison works for\n37\tboth training runs and Data Science Pipelines runs, so data scientists can\n38\titerate across dozens of runs without exporting to spreadsheets.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Multi-run selection on the runs list (two or more runs).\n43\t- A comparison view presenting each selected run's parameters and metrics side\n44\t  by side.\n45\t- A diff presentation of the comparison for two selected runs, highlighting\n46\t  the parameters and metrics whose values differ.\n47\t- The comparison reads run parameters and metrics uniformly for training runs\n48\t  and Data Science Pipelines runs (Data Science Pipelines is a passive\n49\t  component here — no changes are expected in it; its run data is already\n50\t  surfaced through the Dashboard).\n51\t- Comparison is scoped within a single project and cluster; no automatic\n52\t  best-run selection or promotion (explicitly out of scope in the strategy).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given the runs list, when a user selects two or more runs and invokes the\n57\t  comparison action, then a comparison view shows each selected run's\n58\t  parameters and metrics side by side.\n59\t- Given exactly two selected runs, the comparison highlights the parameters\n60\t  and metrics whose values differ between the two runs.\n61\t- Given a mix of training runs and Data Science Pipelines runs, the comparison\n62\t  renders parameters and metrics for both run types correctly (passive\n63\t  validation of Data Science Pipelines: no changes expected there; a failure\n64\t  means the comparison view does not surface run data uniformly).\n65\t- The comparison action and view operate only on runs within the same project\n66\t  and cluster; no cross-project or cross-cluster comparison is offered.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — users can select two or more runs and view their parameters\n71\t  and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n72\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — the run \"diff\" view highlighting which parameters and\n73\t  metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation mode of the same\n74\t  comparison surface and is covered by this epic; the strategy consolidates\n75\t  the two requirements (noted in the decomposition summary as a redundant/\n76\t  overlapping HLR pair, covered at the higher priority).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e298cc7fa9244b","agent_id":"a2addad5e24cf88cd","session_id":"f1c0923d-cf0e-4d69-ac1b-c20ed66527c8","uuid":"0eb08e0e-15c4-44f5-bb9b-345fc04f8773","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:42.362Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1139a8599b4dd4f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
