{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae5f6dd0497ea6b2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Registered model version linkage to producing run\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Registered model version linkage to producing run\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: registered model\n35\tversions record a link back to the run that produced them, and a user can open\n36\tthe run comparison from the Model Registry for a linked version. This gives\n37\tmodel promotion decisions side-by-side visibility into the candidate runs\n38\tbehind registered versions.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Record a reference to the producing run on registered model versions, using\n43\t  the registry's existing extension point for structured metadata on model\n44\t  versions.\n45\t- Surface the run link on the model version through the registry's API so\n46\t  other consumers can resolve a version's producing run.\n47\t- Provide an affordance in the Model Registry view to open the run comparison\n48\t  for a version's linked run, building on the run-comparison capability in the\n49\t  Dashboard (this epic depends on that capability existing).\n50\t- Out of scope: automatic best-run selection or promotion, and comparison\n51\t  across clusters or projects.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- When a model version is registered in the context of a run, the version\n56\t  records a link to that producing run.\n57\t- The run link on a model version is retrievable through the registry's API.\n58\t- Given a registered model version with a run link, when a user opens the\n59\t  comparison from the Model Registry, then the run comparison loads with the\n60\t  linked run selectable alongside other runs of the same project.\n61\t- Versions registered without run context degrade gracefully (no link shown;\n62\t  no error).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — registered model versions link back to the run that\n67\t  produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e298cc7fa9244b","agent_id":"a2addad5e24cf88cd","session_id":"f1c0923d-cf0e-4d69-ac1b-c20ed66527c8","uuid":"3e5c9c08-cb9e-44c8-b099-6736aaabc17b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:43.030Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae5f6dd0497ea6b2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
